5 1-compiler
A compiler converts a high level language into low level language, to be more specific converts source code into byte code which is then executed by the jvm.
2-interpreter
A interpreter executes code line by line, stops when it reaches an error
3-Java virtual machine
after compiler creates bytcode the jvm executes and runs that code.
6 javac (basically is a command that converts or compile your java code ) java(this command runs the code in the jvm)
**7-- logic error(**basically means that your code follows the syntax and runs correctly but not as you want to or doesn't perform what you want it to )   --- syntax error(syntax error basically means you wrote the code incorrectly so that the compiler cant process is such as missing semicolon at the end of print statemnt)









